problem:
Problem description
- This is a single-period land-allocation optimization problem on a farm with total available land $$L$$.
- There is a set of candidate crops $$\mathcal{P}$$, indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, and each crop has a per-acre profit parameter $$\pi_p$$.
- The planning goal is to choose how many acres to assign to each crop so that total profit is maximized.
- There is no demand-driven sales requirement in this instance; the limiting factor is land availability together with crop-mix rules.
- The total planted acreage across all crops cannot exceed the available land $$L$$.
- No more than $$K$$ distinct crop types may be grown.
- Crop selection and acreage must be consistent, meaning that any crop not selected must receive zero acreage.
- There is a set of pairwise land-ratio rules $$\mathcal{R}$$. For each rule, one specified crop must use at least a stated multiple of the acreage of another specified crop.
- A solution is represented by:
    - $$x_p$$: the acreage assigned to crop $$p$$ for each $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$.
    - $$y_p$$: a binary indicator equal to $$1$$ if crop $$p$$ is grown and $$0$$ otherwise.
    - $$Z$$: the total profit obtained from the chosen land allocation.

Input Format
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "description": "Single planning period with $$|\\mathcal{T}|=1$$."
  },
  "crops": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$",
    "description": "Array of crop identifiers; the number of crops is $$|\\mathcal{P}|$$."
  },
  "profit_per_acre": {
    "symbol": "$$\\pi \\in \\mathbb{R}_+^{|\\mathcal{P}|}$$",
    "description": "Per-acre profit vector, where $$\\pi_p$$ is the profit earned per acre of crop $$p$$."
  },
  "land_capacity": {
    "symbol": "$$L$$",
    "description": "Total available land in acres."
  },
  "max_distinct_crops": {
    "symbol": "$$K$$",
    "description": "Maximum number of crop types that may be grown."
  },
  "ratio_rules": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{R}$$",
    "description": "Array of pairwise acreage rules. Each rule contains $$i$$, $$j$$, and $$\\alpha_{ij}$$, meaning crop $$i$$ must be grown on at least $$\\alpha_{ij}$$ times the acreage of crop $$j$$."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "acreage_by_crop": {
    "symbol": "$$x \\in \\mathbb{R}_+^{|\\mathcal{P}|}$$",
    "description": "Acreage assigned to each crop, listed in the same order as $$\\mathcal{P}$$."
  },
  "selected_crop_indicator": {
    "symbol": "$$y \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|\\mathcal{P}|}$$",
    "description": "Binary selection vector, where $$y_p=1$$ indicates that crop $$p$$ is grown."
  },
  "total_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$Z$$",
    "description": "Maximum achievable profit for the chosen allocation."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "crop_order": ["apples", "pears", "oranges", "lemons"],
  "profit_per_acre": ["$$2000$$", "$$1800$$", "$$2200$$", "$$3000$$"],
  "land_capacity": "$$120$$",
  "max_distinct_crops": "$$2$$",
  "ratio_rules": [
    {
      "lhs_crop": "apples",
      "rhs_crop": "pears",
      "minimum_multiple": "$$2$$"
    },
    {
      "lhs_crop": "apples",
      "rhs_crop": "lemons",
      "minimum_multiple": "$$3$$"
    },
    {
      "lhs_crop": "oranges",
      "rhs_crop": "lemons",
      "minimum_multiple": "$$2$$"
    }
  ]
}
